  "verbalization": "Arundinol B is shown to have a target relationship with SNU-387, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. All these compounds ultimately target LNCaP, suggesting a potential pathway where Arundinol B may influence LNCaP through a series of molecular interactions involving SNU-387. The evidence implies that Arundinol B could act as a modulator or activator of SNU-387, which then exerts its effects on LNCaP. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on SNU-387, which may be a key mediator in the biological activity of Arundinol B against LNCaP. The mechanism is supported by the shared target relationship between SNU-387 and LNCaP, suggesting a potential role for SNU-387 in the pharmacological action of Arundinol B.",
